					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13946081#post-4848916</guid>
				<title>SCP-5925: Re: +1</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13946081/scp-5925#post-4848916</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2020 23:53:09 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TheSlothSavant</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2192823</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Real glad to hear that! I realize making a character of popular culture into an SCP is hokey if not done well. I wouldn't have even attempted it if not for A. My recent delve into the many different folklore/mythological entities that make up our current understanding of Saint Nick, and B. The association with the fae that came to me. I figured making him a fae was the only solid way to do it.</p> <p>So its relieving to know my attempts were not in vain!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
